    "text": "The characteristic X-rays wavelength is related to atomic number by the relation<br />\r<br />\r<math><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ν</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\r<br />\rWhen Z is the atomic number, a and b are Mosley's constants. If <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2.886</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2.365</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> corresponding to <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math> respectively, the value of Z corresponding to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.660</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> is"
